Verified: deleteFromDownloadQueue (MessagesStorage.java:11183-11210)
posts cancelDownloading on the UI thread, and cancelDownloading had no
pin check at all — only FileLoader.cancelLoadFiles (plural) has the
isFileNamePinned guard, and this path never goes through it. An edit
of a message whose old media is still downloading therefore cancelled
that download, stranding the freeze copy. Fix: skip any pair whose
resolved attach file name is pinned (mirror-only lookup, UI-safe),
mirroring the cancelLoadFiles guard. The deferred cancel is already
recorded as a DeferredDelete row by Layer 1 and fires at release.
Supporting fixes: mirrorRemoveForRef now only clears the shared
file-name mirror when no other active ref still names the file (new
PreservedRefDao.getActiveRefsForFileName; fan-out LIVE + EDIT pin on
one download must keep the name pinned until both are done); purge
and settings-clear reorder mirror cleanup to run after the bulk row
delete, so the DAO re-check does not see doomed rows as still active.
